CLASS:: KSMixer
summary:: The group, bus and insert topology of one EventScheduler play
categories:: Scheduling
related:: Classes/EventScheduler

DESCRIPTION::
Builds, message for message and in the same order as SuperSonic's code::setupTracks::, one score group at the head of the root node holding every track (parent, source group, effects group, two buses one channel per speaker), main last at the widest declared width, the insert chains or bypass routers, the summing routers, and main's output stage: the binaural decoder (code::\fold::), the hardware array mirror (code::\array::) or a stereo router. Frees exactly that group on stop or ring-out. Bus numbers come from the server's own allocator.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: spatialPlan
Validate code::meta.spatial:: and decide widths, geometry and the output def. Every refusal throws before any node exists.

METHOD:: build
METHOD:: freeNow
METHOD:: detach

METHOD:: trackInfo
Per track: code::parentGroup, srcGroup, fxGroup, srcBus, fxBus, width, insertNodes, routerNode::.

METHOD:: gains
METHOD:: mutes
METHOD:: solos
METHOD:: applyGain
METHOD:: effectiveGain
Router gains (fader, mute, solo) that persist across builds.

METHOD:: setupStemTaps
Hardware stem taps after each summing router: stereo routers, or with code::binaural:: the per-track decoders on the geometry buffer.

METHOD:: setupStemDecoders
The per-track decoders onto private stereo buses, for code::record(binaural: true)::; returns name -> Bus.

METHOD:: setupMeters
